azapi_update_resource - remove vm from defender for cloud fails

Use case:
* we are adding a defender for cloud server workload protection plan to individual virtual machines 
* at some point we would like to remove some servers from the plan

Based on https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/defender-for-cloud/tutorial-enable-servers-plan#enable-defender-for-servers-at-the-resource-level-at-scale,
in order to add servers we use the following terraform code:

```hcl
resource "azapi_update_resource" "example" {
  type = "Microsoft.Security/pricings@2024-01-01"
  name = "VirtualMachines"
  parent_id = "/subscriptions/somesubscription/resourceGroups/someresourcegroup/providers/Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines/somevm"

 body = {
     properties = {
       pricingTier = "Standard",
       subPlan     = "P1"
     }
  }
}
```

This works fine.

But as soon as we try to remove this server from the plan with the following code change:

```hcl
resource "azapi_update_resource" "example" {
  type = "Microsoft.Security/pricings@2024-01-01"
  name = "VirtualMachines"
  parent_id = "/subscriptions/somesubscription/resourceGroups/someresourcegroup/providers/Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines/somevm"

 body = {
     properties = {
       pricingTier = "Free"
     }
  }
}
```

The azapi provider still submits the original property `subPlan` with value `P1` which results in the error:

```
{
│   "error": {
│     "code": "InvalidInputJson",
│     "message": "The 'SubPlan' property is not supported for pricing tier 'Free'."
│   }
│ }
```

We know that the azapi provider still includes the original `subPlan` property because we inspected the trace log:

```
"body":"{\"name\":\"VirtualMachines\",\"properties\":{\"extensions\":[{\"isEnabled\":\"False\",\"name\":\"MdeDesignatedSubscription\"}],\"pricingTier\":\"Free\",\"subPlan\":\"P1\"}}"
```

If we run `Free` freshly without any backing state, this runs fine.

`azapi_update_resource` with `Microsoft.App/managedEnvironments@2025-02-02-preview` doesn't set `headers` if using `sensitive_body`

Terraform Version: `v1.12.2`
AzApi Version: `2.5.0`

When trying to update the Azure Container App Environment OTel Endpoints via an `azapi_update_resource` using `sensitive_body` for the `headers` property which would contain sensitive API keys. The merge-patch seems to be setting the property value as `null` but its type is an array or maps of Key/Value properties as per the Azure API spec for `Microsoft.App/managedEnvironments@2025-02-02-preview`: https://github.com/Azure/azure-rest-api-specs/blob/9e82d503ceec8ab4248587d066e1702608bb33ab/specification/app/resource-manager/Microsoft.App/preview/2025-02-02-preview/examples/ManagedEnvironments_CreateOrUpdate.json#L38

I validated that the data structure expected by the API spec matches what i'm supplying in the `headers` property that im setting in the `sensitive_body` but when I apply, there are no errors but the value is `null`.

I validated this by just setting it in the `body` propery (so no merge-patching) and it works so suspect there is something odd happening when supplying a property thats not just a simple string etc

What am I doing wrong here or is this a bug.

