bug(azapi_resource): using `sensitive_body` with ephemeral values causes configuration not to be idempotent

Hi @ms-henglu

Thanks very much for the 2.4 release! I have been experimenting with write-only attributes and have found that the configuration is never idempotent. It is obvious why this is but I think there needs to be a way of avoiding it.

In AzureRM and other HashiCorp providers, they have the concept of [`value_wo_version`](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/hashicorp/azurerm/4.28.0/docs/resources/key_vault_secret#value_wo_version-3). This value of this is actually just checked for [any  change](https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform-provider-azurerm/blob/cb20d9de96b920867b5aa1c7741e90b69fcd0a8a/internal/services/keyvault/key_vault_secret_resource.go#L290).

### Repro config

```terraform
ephemeral "random_password" "secret_value" {
  length  = 16
}

resource "azapi_resource" "secret" {
  parent_id = var.parent_id
  type      = "Microsoft.KeyVault/vaults/secrets@2024-11-01"
  name      = var.name
  body = {
    properties = {
      contentType = var.content_type
      attributes = {
        enabled = true
      }
    }
    tags = var.tags
  }
  sensitive_body = {
    properties = {
      value = ephemeral.random_password.secret_value
    }
  }
}
```

When using the above with a standard variable (stored in state) then the resource is idempotent. When using an ephemeral input then the resource is updated every time.

### Proposal

Create a new dynamic attribute that, when changed, causes the sensitive body to be considered as changed. Specifying `null` would leave the behaviour as-is.

E.g.

```terraform
resource "azapi_resource" "secret" {
  parent_id = var.parent_id
  type      = "Microsoft.KeyVault/vaults/secrets@2024-11-01"
  name      = var.name
  body = {
    properties = {
      contentType = var.content_type
      attributes = {
        enabled = true
      }
    }
    tags = var.tags
  }
  sensitive_body = {
    properties = {
      value = ephemeral.random_password.secret_value
    }
  }
  sensitive_body_replace_triggers = some.input.that.indicates.a.change
}
```

WDYT?

